  steps: [
    { math: '1 · Elastic rebound', note: 'Plates lock, strain accumulates for centuries, then the fault snaps — the earthquake is the release. The elastic energy stored in rock becomes the shaking (the physics ladder\'s springs, at geological scale).' },
    { math: '2 · Waves carry the message', note: 'P-waves (fast, push–pull — arrive first), S-waves (slower, shear — cannot cross liquid), surface waves (slowest, most damaging). The interior lesson: seismology reads the planet from quake echoes.' },
    { math: '3 · Magnitude vs intensity', note: 'Magnitude (moment magnitude now, not Richter) = energy released — one number per quake, log scale (each step ≈ 32× energy). Intensity (Modified Mercalli) = shaking experienced — varies by location; the same quake ruins one town and rattles another.' },
    { math: '4 · The destructive sequence', note: 'Shaking → building collapse (most deaths), fires, landslides, liquefaction (soil turns liquid), tsunamis (subsea quakes — 2004 Indian Ocean ~228,000 dead; early-warning systems since saved thousands).' },
